(GALE ENCYCLOPEDIA OF MEDICINE) '
(RESPIRATORY DISORDERS, ASTHMA AND BRONCHITIS) '
() '
(Pulmonary Medicine, Airway Hyperreactivity & Bronchospasm) '
() '
(Definition: Asthma and bronchitis are common inflammatory airway conditions) '
(causing recurrent episodes of wheezing, breathlessness, chest tightness, and) '
(coughing, linked to reversible bronchial hyperreactivity and mucus hypersecretion.) '
() '
(Etiology and Environmental Triggers: Bronchial inflammation triggers smooth muscle) '
(constriction around the bronchioles, mucosal edema, and tenacious mucus plug) '
(formation. Key triggers include viral respiratory pathogens, airborne) '
(aeroallergens \(dust mites, pollen, animal dander\), cold dry air, physical) '
(exertion, airborne irritants \(tobacco smoke, chemical fumes\), and emotional) '
(hyperventilation.) '
() '
(Immediate Action and Relief Protocol: At the first sign of respiratory tightness:) '
(1\) Sit upright immediately; never recline; 2\) Eliminate exposure to active) '
(triggers; 3\) Utilize prescribed fast-acting bronchodilator rescue inhalers \(such) '
(as albuterol\) with a spacer as directed by a physician; 4\) Practice pursed-lip) '
(breathing to prevent dynamic airway collapse during expiration.) '
() '
(Warning Signs Requiring Emergency Medical Care: Call emergency medical services) '
(immediately if breathing difficulty causes inability to complete full sentences) '
(without pausing, severe retractions \(chest wall sinking in\), blue or gray) '
(discoloration around the lips or fingernails \(cyanosis\), or when rescue) '
(bronchodilators fail to provide prompt relief.) '
() '
ET
endstream
endobj
