(GALE ENCYCLOPEDIA OF MEDICINE) '
(INFECTIOUS ILLNESSES, FEVER AND VIRAL INFECTIONS) '
() '
(Infectious Disease, Thermoregulation & Upper Respiratory Illness) '
() '
(Definition: Fever \(pyrexia\) is a regulated elevation of the internal body core) '
(temperature above the normal physiological baseline \(typically > 38.0 C or 100.4) '
(F\), orchestrated by the preoptic anterior hypothalamus in response to infectious) '
(or inflammatory pyrogens.) '
() '
(Mechanisms and Immune Defense Role: Exogenous microbial toxins stimulate host) '
(leukocytes and macrophages to release endogenous pyrogenic cytokines) '
(\(interleukin-1, interleukin-6, TNF-alpha\). These induce hypothalamic prostaglandin) '
(E2 \(PGE2\) synthesis, shifting the thermal set-point upward to enhance leukocyte) '
(phagocytosis, inhibit viral replication, and mobilize antimicrobial defenses.) '
() '
(Evidence-Based Relief and Hydration Care: Supportive care focuses on comfort and) '
(systemic hydration: 1\) Drink plentiful fluids \(oral rehydration salts, broths,) '
(dilute juices\) to offset insensible fluid losses from sweating and tachypnea; 2\)) '
(Rest in a well-ventilated, temperate environment with light clothing; 3\) Apply) '
(cool or lukewarm damp compresses to the forehead and neck; 4\) Over-the-counter) '
(antipyretics \(acetaminophen or ibuprofen\) may be used strictly according to) '
(package instructions to relieve discomfort.) '
() '
(Warning Signs Requiring Urgent Medical Evaluation: Seek emergency medical) '
(evaluation if fever exceeds 39.5 C \(103.1 F\), persists beyond 72 hours, or is) '
(accompanied by stiff neck and photophobia \(concerning for meningitis\), new) '
(petechial rash, persistent vomiting, extreme lethargy, confusion, or difficulty) '
(breathing.) '
() '
ET
endstream
endobj
