(GALE ENCYCLOPEDIA OF MEDICINE) '
(DERMATOLOGICAL DISORDERS, ECZEMA AND ALLERGIC RASHES) '
() '
(Dermatology, Epidermal Barrier Dysfunction & Pruritus) '
() '
(Definition: Eczema \(atopic dermatitis\) and allergic contact dermatitis are chronic) '
(inflammatory skin disorders characterized by pruritus \(intense itching\), erythema,) '
(xerosis \(dryness\), and excoriated eczematous lesions.) '
() '
(Pathophysiological Etiology: Genetic defects in epidermal barrier proteins \(such) '
(as filaggrin\) increase transepidermal water loss and facilitate environmental) '
(antigen penetration, triggering hyperreactive cutaneous immune responses and local) '
(mast cell degranulation.) '
() '
(Immediate Relief and Soothing Care: 1\) Apply thick, fragrance-free ceramide-rich) '
(emollient ointments immediately after lukewarm bathing \(the 'soak and seal') '
(method\); 2\) Apply cold, damp cloth compresses to pruritic patches for 10-15) '
(minutes to soothe nerve endings; 3\) Keep fingernails trimmed short to minimize) '
(mechanical skin excoriation and secondary bacterial infection.) '
() '
(Warning Signs Requiring Clinical Attention: Consult a physician if rash spreads) '
(rapidly across large body surface areas, develops yellow honey-colored crusting or) '
(oozing pus \(impetigo\), exhibits severe pain or swelling, or if accompanied by high) '
(systemic fever or facial swelling.) '
() '
ET
endstream
endobj
