(GALE ENCYCLOPEDIA OF MEDICINE) '
(SPINAL DISORDERS, LUMBAR BACK PAIN AND ERGONOMICS) '
() '
(Spinal Biomechanics, Paraspinal Spasm & Ergonomic Care) '
() '
(Definition: Low back pain \(lumbago\) refers to discomfort localized between the) '
(lower costal margin and the inferior gluteal folds, representing one of the) '
(leading global causes of activity limitation and occupational disability.) '
() '
(Common Causes and Biomechanical Stress: Over 85 percent of back pain episodes are) '
(non-specific musculoskeletal strains involving paraspinal muscles, ligaments, and) '
(facet joints. Contributing factors include prolonged static sitting, poor) '
(workstation ergonomics, heavy unergonomic lifting, sudden spinal rotational) '
(torque, core abdominal muscular weakness, and intervertebral disc degeneration.) '
() '
(Immediate Self-Care and Relief Measures: 1\) Relative Rest: Avoid strict prolonged) '
(bed rest \(which stiffens spinal joints and delays functional recovery\); maintain) '
(gentle daily ambulation; 2\) Postural Positioning: Rest in a comfortable supine) '
(position with knees bent and supported by pillows, or in a reclined semi-Fowler's) '
(posture; 3\) Thermal Therapy: Apply ice packs for the first 48 hours for acute) '
(spasm, followed by soothing moist heat packs to relax hypertonic muscular bands.) '
() '
(Urgent Neurological Warning Signs \(Red Flags\): Seek immediate emergency) '
(neurosurgical evaluation if back pain is accompanied by loss of bowel or bladder) '
(control \(cauda equina syndrome\), progressive sensory numbness in the) '
(groin/perineal region \(saddle anesthesia\), or progressive motor weakness in the) '
(legs \(such as foot drop\).) '
() '
ET
endstream
endobj
