(GALE ENCYCLOPEDIA OF MEDICINE) '
(PREVENTATIVE HEALTH, CLINICAL NUTRITION AND IMMUNE HEALTH) '
() '
(Health Promotion, Preventative Medicine & Lifestyle Science) '
() '
(Definition: Preventative medicine and lifestyle health encompass evidence-based) '
(strategies designed to protect physiological homeostasis, bolster innate and) '
(adaptive immune resilience, and mitigate chronic disease risks before clinical) '
(onset occurs.) '
() '
(Core Pillars of Cellular and Systemic Health: 1\) Balanced Mediterranean-Style) '
(Nutrition emphasizing diverse polyphenol-rich plant foods, lean proteins, and) '
(omega-3 fatty acids; 2\) Regular Aerobic and Resistance Exercise \(150 minutes of) '
(moderate activity weekly\) to enhance cardiovascular fitness, metabolic insulin) '
(sensitivity, and immune cell recirculation; 3\) Restorative Sleep \(7 to 9 hours) '
(nightly\) essential for endocrine balance and tissue repair; 4\) Stress Modulation) '
(via mindfulness and social connection to suppress chronic pro-inflammatory) '
(cortisol elevation.) '
() '
(Clinical Preventative Screening Guidelines: Routine periodic health checkups with) '
(a licensed primary care physician should include blood pressure assessment,) '
(fasting lipid profiles, hemoglobin A1c monitoring, body mass index tracking, and) '
(age-appropriate cancer screenings.) '
() '
ET
endstream
endobj
